{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Expose node1's staged projects directory as an authenticated SMB share named projects for the design team.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The projects share maps to the required directory, permits only designer, disables guest access and SMB1, uses persistent SELinux labeling, and remains active and enabled after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b09053adcc0044f7","cmd-1e96dd81f31d48be","cmd-4cdc6f0abbc54fae","cmd-5e3cd70ff58c4793"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow node2 to list, read, and update project documents as designer using the demonstration credentials.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct node2 SMB operations authenticated as designer, listed and read existing documents, created and overwrote a document, and verified its final content on node1, including after both restarts. The Samba account password was populated from access.txt.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b09053adcc0044f7","cmd-5443395b63c04991","cmd-f5acc67b4d6f482e","cmd-3361c48860604f27"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Reject guest access and access to sibling directories or files.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Guest tree connection and anonymous enumeration were denied; the private sibling was not exported; and authenticated parent traversal and sibling-file retrieval both failed without creating a local file.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5443395b63c04991","cmd-f5acc67b4d6f482e","cmd-2b1b7e0181df4821","cmd-5e3cd70ff58c4793"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the initial drawings in /srv/legacy2/samba-team-share intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final SHA-256 hashes for drawing.txt and materials.csv exactly match the preparation baseline and the executor's pre-change hashes, including after restart and remote update testing.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-602da82895a447b6","cmd-4cdc6f0abbc54fae","cmd-5e3cd70ff58c4793","cmd-3361c48860604f27"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on CentOS Stream 10 with kernel 6.12.0-205.el10.x86_64. Samba and client packages were installed from the platform's native CentOS repositories, and final package-health checks passed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f9cf9f6e4fc84c31","cmd-259e3884b8ed48c8","cmd-469abddd041a4ce0","cmd-ab88af3aef2747b3","cmd-f5acc67b4d6f482e","cmd-5e3cd70ff58c4793","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.94,"summary":"No causally unnecessary managed-system mutation was identified: package installation, account and share configuration, permission and SELinux changes, firewall/service enablement, update files, and restarts all supported implementation or bounded verification. Both restart protocols were complete and independently corroborated: each node had a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered functionality. Hygiene is reduced slightly because evidence artifacts remained in /tmp: /tmp/testparm.out on node1 and eleven SMB test/readback files on node2. These were created by the verification commands and were not cleaned up. No failed services or damaged package state remained.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1e96dd81f31d48be","cmd-5443395b63c04991","cmd-5d2fb2bdb55849b6","cmd-9b0cb41929094280","cmd-7ed7221c9f6a47b6","cmd-f5acc67b4d6f482e","cmd-39578a3bd23e470a","cmd-17eb463520e14d3a","cmd-4cdc6f0abbc54fae","cmd-f60319cc3c634d9f","cmd-73226563ddf7441e","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_prepare:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral and final-state evidence. The SMB share works from node2 for authenticated listing, reading, and updating; unauthorized access is rejected; original drawings remain checksum-identical; and the OS and kernel were retained. Provider-wide restart evidence is complete and consistent for both nodes. Only minor temporary verification-file residue detracts from operational hygiene.","limitations":["The demonstration password is redacted in captured output, so its literal equality across access.txt, Samba provisioning, and the node2 SMB_PASS environment cannot be independently compared; the command flow and successful authentication provide strong indirect linkage.","Lifecycle temporary-file inventories are bounded; they directly establish the listed residue but may not enumerate files outside the collector's scope."]}
